For every $n\geq20$,
\begin{equation}
 a_n=\sum_{j=0}^{17}c_j a_{n-18+j},
\end{equation}
where the coefficients, in increasing order of $j$, are
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
(c_0,\ldots,c_{17})={}&(-25,240,204,-6334,6468,42628,\\
 &-83203,-34136,160400,-40816,-108224,56184,\\
 &23849,-19128,340,1854,-436,36).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
At $n=19$, the left side of~\eqref{eq:recurrence} minus its right side is
$864$. Its minimal eventual homogeneous constant-coefficient recurrence
order over $\Q$ is eighteen.

The number of labelled height-$n$ colourings with exactly one defect is
$uM^{n-1}v$. Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 6a_n=uM^{n-1}v\qquad(n\geq1).
\end{equation}
